BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-191157@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T173000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260622T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260622T190000
SUMMARY:TEDxBoston: Visions of the Next 250 - A First Look
LOCATION:The Reading Room
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 120 spots le
 ft\nStatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events
 /191157\n\n5:30PM Reception\, 6:00PM Discussion \nFor 250 years\, Massach
 usetts has been a place where bold ideas take root. On June 22nd\, the eve
 ning before the Visions of the Next 250 gathering at GBH\, we invite membe
 rs to a private preview in The Reading Room to explore a more challenging 
 question: what will the next 250 years look like\, and who is shaping them
 ?\n\nJohn Werner\, venture capitalist\, MIT lecturer\, and Forbes AI colum
 nist\, will interview four people working at the frontier of science\, med
 icine\, education\, ethics\, and intelligence in the kind of off-the-recor
 d conversation that needs fewer chairs to go deeper.\n\nTogether\, they wi
 ll explore some of the defining questions of our time: where machine intel
 ligence is headed and what it asks of us\; how wearable technology and dat
 a are transforming our understanding of health\, resilience\, and human pe
 rformance\; how society can thoughtfully navigate the ethical challenges t
 hat accompany powerful new technologies\; and how education and lifelong l
 earning must evolve to prepare future generations for a world increasingly
  shaped by innovation and artificial intelligence.\n\nSpeakers include:\n\
 nAlham Saadat - Executive Director\, The Innovation Trail of Greater Bosto
 n\nAlex Wissner-Gross - Investor & Entrepreneur\nEmily Capodilupo - Senior
  Vice President of Research\, Algorithms\, and Data\, WHOOP\nJoseph Aoun -
  President\, Northeastern University\n\n*This event is complimentary and r
 eserved for members\, plus one guest. Light bites and refreshments will be
  served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/191157
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
