BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-189486@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260625T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260625T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260625T183000
SUMMARY:Meet the Maker: Rhonda Kallman from Boston Harbor Distillery
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\n
 Event URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/189486\n\nJoin us for a
  spirited evening celebrating 250 years of Massachusetts in partnership wi
 th Boston Harbor Distillery. Led by founder Rhonda Kallman\, this receptio
 n-style Meet the Maker invites members to explore the stories\, craftsmans
 hip\, and local history woven into one of Boston’s most distinctive dist
 illeries—where every detail\, from the spirits themselves to the names o
 n the bottles\, reflects a deep connection to place.\n\nA pioneering force
  in the craft beverage industry\, Rhonda Kallman has spent decades shaping
  the future of American brewing and distilling. Her passion for whiskey\, 
 storytelling\, and craftsmanship is at the heart of Boston Harbor Distille
 ry’s approach: honoring history while redefining what modern American sp
 irits can be.\n\nGuided by Rhonda\, members will have the first opportunit
 y to taste an exclusive selections from Boston Harbor Distillery including
 : Putnam Single Malt Whiskey & Rye Expressions\, Demon Seed Whiskey and fe
 aturing American 250 Custom Malt Whiskey\, of which only one barrel was pr
 oduced. Set within the legacy of a restored 19th-century waterfront mill b
 uilding in Dorchester\, the distillery has become a modern landmark of Ame
 rican craft spirits—equal parts innovation\, heritage\, and unapologetic
  Boston character.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for member
 s only. Complimentary light bites will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/189486
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage
END:VEVENT
