BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-191160@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260630T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260630T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260630T183000
SUMMARY:Rethinking Women's Health: Mental Health & Modern Life
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: Health & Wellness\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 80 spot
 s left\nStatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/ev
 ents/191160\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion \nMental health is fi
 nally getting the attention it deserves—but the conversation is only beg
 inning.\n\nJoin us for the fourth installment of Rethinking Women's Health
 \, our ongoing series exploring the evolving landscape of women's well-bei
 ng through the lens of today's leading physicians\, researchers\, and advo
 cates. This session turns its focus to mental health\, examining the inter
 section of mind\, body\, identity\, and culture while challenging outdated
  approaches to care.\n\nEach speaker will bring one topic to the conversat
 ion\, offering a distinct perspective on women's mental health today. Topi
 cs will include trauma-informed care and ketamine-assisted psychotherapy\,
  the realities of navigating modern womanhood in a rapidly changing cultur
 al landscape\, and the structural and psychological factors that make ment
 al wellness both deeply personal and profoundly complex.\n\nLeading the di
 scussion are Dr. Cecil R. Webster Jr.\, Harvard-trained psychiatrist\, psy
 choanalyst\, and founder of Webster Clinic\; Dr. Marni Chanoff\, Harvard-t
 rained psychiatrist\, educator\, and founder of Joy In Health\; and Dr. J
 ackie Buchanan\, Harvard-trained child\, adolescent\, and adult psychiatr
 ist.\n\nDesigned to offer practical tools\, fresh perspectives\, and meani
 ngful insights\, the evening will conclude with 30 minutes of audience dis
 cussion and Q&A. We encourage attendees to bring their own questions and c
 uriosities as we create a thoughtful space for open and engaging conversat
 ion.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Compli
 mentary light bites will be served\, and beverages will be available for p
 urchase.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/191160
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness
END:VEVENT
